00:44:23.226 --> 00:44:24.726
No.


00:44:25.826 --> 00:44:28.626
It has everything to do with Michael.


00:44:32.827 --> 00:44:34.527
Happy's good.


00:44:35.227 --> 00:44:37.427
You know what I think we should do?


00:44:37.427 --> 00:44:40.427
We should start a charity
for kids like Michael.


00:44:40.427 --> 00:44:41.227
Okay.


00:44:41.227 --> 00:44:43.828
- Maybe fund a program at Wingate.
- Sure.


00:44:43.828 --> 00:44:46.528
Lord knows that school
could use a little color.


00:44:46.628 --> 00:44:50.128
Michael's like a flying and milking
that place.


00:44:50.428 --> 00:44:52.628
Are you listening to me?


00:44:55.529 --> 00:45:02.829
I try to concentrate on one...
thing... at a time.


00:45:03.929 --> 00:45:07.030
You knew I was multi-tasker
when you married me, right?


00:45:07.130 --> 00:45:10.430
- I sure did.
- Alright. Okay. Let's check it.


00:45:14.830 --> 00:45:18.731
Okay. Tuohy family.
Big smiles everyone!


00:45:19.931 --> 00:45:23.331
And, one , two, three...


00:45:26.432 --> 00:45:29.832
Michael! Michael come over here
and get in the next one.


00:45:29.832 --> 00:45:33.032
Come on. Come on. Come over here.


00:45:38.333 --> 00:45:41.533
Oh, come on. It's not like I'm gonna
put it on the Christmas card.


00:45:41.633 --> 00:45:45.733
Okay, let's scootch in a little tighter.


00:45:45.933 --> 00:45:47.534
That's good.


00:45:48.334 --> 00:45:49.834
Really big smiles.


00:45:49.934 --> 00:45:53.534
Okay, one, two three... say Rebels!


00:45:53.634 --> 00:45:55.134
"Rebels"


00:45:58.435 --> 00:46:03.935
TV commentary


00:46:03.935 --> 00:46:05.435
I got it.


00:46:06.335 --> 00:46:08.836
- Who's winning?
- Tennessee.


00:46:09.436 --> 00:46:11.536
- Who are they playing?
- Clemson.


00:46:11.536 --> 00:46:14.036
Your mom roots against Tennessee
no matter who they're playing?


00:46:14.036 --> 00:46:16.836
Oh, yes, I do. With gusto.


00:46:16.936 --> 00:46:19.036
She can't stand Tennessee.


00:46:19.136 --> 00:46:22.337
Collie-bell, I thought you were
going to your boyfriend's?


00:46:22.337 --> 00:46:25.237
I thought of hanging around here today.


00:46:26.737 --> 00:46:28.337
I like that.


00:46:28.537 --> 00:46:31.338
Hey, baby. There's a coupla messages
on the machine but I didn't check 'em.


00:46:31.438 --> 00:46:32.938
Alright.


00:46:33.938 --> 00:46:37.438
Hey, Sean, hey, Leigh Anne,
It's cousin Bobby. Happy New Years!


00:46:37.538 --> 00:46:39.538
Listen, I've had about five cold ones...


00:46:39.538 --> 00:46:43.239
- Of course she had. - So I'm...
I'm just gonna go ahead and ask...


00:46:43.339 --> 00:46:46.639
Ya'll know there's a colored boy
in your Christmas Card?


00:46:49.739 --> 00:46:50.939
What?


00:46:51.940 --> 00:46:57.440
You just looked teeny-tiny next to him.
Right? Like Jessica Lange and King Kong.


00:46:58.540 --> 00:47:01.240
Hey, does Michael get the family discount
at Taco Bell?


00:47:01.240 --> 00:47:04.741
Because if he does Sean's gonna lose
a few stores.


00:47:05.041 --> 00:47:06.241
He's a great kid.


00:47:06.341 --> 00:47:09.641
Well, I say make it official
and just adopt him.


00:47:11.041 --> 00:47:12.441
He's gonna be eighteen
in a few months.


00:47:12.441 --> 00:47:15.842
Doesn't really make much sense
to legally adopt.


00:47:18.442 --> 00:47:22.242
Leigh Anne, is this some
sort of white guilt thing?


00:47:22.942 --> 00:47:25.143
What will your daddy say?


00:47:25.643 --> 00:47:29.143
Umm... before or after he turns over
in his grave?


00:47:29.243 --> 00:47:31.743
Daddy's been gone five years Elaine,


00:47:31.843 --> 00:47:34.043
make matters worse you were
at the funeral.


00:47:34.143 --> 00:47:37.544
Remember? You wore Chanel
and that awful black hat.


00:47:37.644 --> 00:47:39.544
Look, here's the deal.


00:47:39.544 --> 00:47:42.644
I don't need y'all to approve
my choices, alright?


00:47:43.044 --> 00:47:45.445
But I do ask you to respect them.


00:47:45.445 --> 00:47:47.445
You've no idea what this boy's
been through.


00:47:47.445 --> 00:47:50.245
And If this is going to be
some running diatribe


00:47:50.245 --> 00:47:53.845
I can find an overpriced salad
a lot closer to home.


00:47:55.045 --> 00:47:56.846
Leigh Anne, I'm so sorry.
We didn't intend to---


00:47:56.946 --> 00:47:58.446
No. We didn't really.


00:47:58.546 --> 00:48:01.746
I think, what you're doing is so great.


00:48:01.946 --> 00:48:04.546
To open up your home... to him.


00:48:05.046 --> 00:48:08.047
Honey, you're changing that boy's life.


00:48:08.147 --> 00:48:09.347
No.


00:48:10.347 --> 00:48:12.247
He's changing mine.


00:48:13.447 --> 00:48:16.747
That's awesome for you,
but what about Collins?


00:48:17.648 --> 00:48:18.848
What about Collins?


00:48:18.848 --> 00:48:21.748
Aren't you worried, I mean,
even just a little?


00:48:21.848 --> 00:48:24.148
He's a boy, a large, black boy,


00:48:24.248 --> 00:48:26.648
sleeping under the same roof.


00:48:29.149 --> 00:48:30.749
Shame on you.


00:48:35.449 --> 00:48:37.149
I've got this.


00:48:39.150 --> 00:48:41.350
Be honest with me, okay?


00:48:42.850 --> 00:48:46.150
Is Michael being here making
you uncomfortable?


00:48:47.150 --> 00:48:50.451
They're stupid kids,
who cares what they say.


00:48:50.751 --> 00:48:51.951
What kids?


00:48:52.051 --> 00:48:53.451
At school.


00:48:54.451 --> 00:48:55.751
They're juvenile.


00:48:55.751 --> 00:48:58.551
And what do they juvenile kids say?


00:48:58.951 --> 00:49:01.552
It's really not worth repeating.


00:49:02.252 --> 00:49:06.052
And don't worry about SJ;
he likes all the attention.


00:49:06.652 --> 00:49:09.652
He introduces Michael
as his big brother.


00:49:13.453 --> 00:49:16.253
- What about you?
- It's fine.


00:49:19.053 --> 00:49:22.354
I mean, you can't just throw him
out on the street.


00:49:22.354 --> 00:49:24.854
I can make other arrangements.


00:49:28.454 --> 00:49:29.954
- Hi, Mike.
- Hi.


00:49:30.054 --> 00:49:32.054
- Need a push?
-Yeah.


00:49:38.555 --> 00:49:40.255
Higher, Mike! Higher!


00:49:44.056 --> 00:49:45.556
Higher!


00:49:50.556 --> 00:49:52.056
Higher!


00:49:56.257 --> 00:49:58.857
Don't look down.
Don't look down!


00:50:32.660 --> 00:50:35.060
- Where are you going?
- Collins?


00:50:47.261 --> 00:50:49.662
Quit looking at me like that.


00:50:49.762 --> 00:50:52.462
I mean, we study together at home.


00:51:09.263 --> 00:51:13.964
You know how much those things weigh?
This kid's gonna make us all famous.


00:51:15.364 --> 00:51:17.264
Easy, Bert, man.
It's only the spring


00:51:17.264 --> 00:51:19.764
he hasn't even been through
his first practice yet.


00:51:19.764 --> 00:51:21.565
No. He's a player.


00:51:24.465 --> 00:51:26.065
Ready.


00:51:26.865 --> 00:51:28.665
Get down, son.
Get down in your stands.


00:51:28.765 --> 00:51:30.265
In your stands!


00:51:30.865 --> 00:51:32.066
Go!


00:51:37.866 --> 00:51:39.466
Mike! Son!


00:51:40.166 --> 00:51:43.467
You fall off the block and then
you wanna shuck-shuck the blocker.


00:51:43.567 --> 00:51:46.367
Right? Shuck it!
Alright? Let's go!


00:51:49.367 --> 00:51:50.767
Papa?


00:51:52.067 --> 00:51:53.868
How's he doing?


00:51:53.968 --> 00:51:56.468
Doesn't quite have
the hang of it yet.


00:52:02.868 --> 00:52:04.569
Hey, Mike. Son...


00:52:04.869 --> 00:52:07.169
Shuck the blocker. Don't hold him!


00:52:10.569 --> 00:52:13.970
No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No.


00:52:25.171 --> 00:52:27.271
Balloons! There are balloons!


00:52:27.671 --> 00:52:30.571
Guys, quit looking at the balloons.
Everybody.


00:52:30.671 --> 00:52:33.771
Most kids from bad situations
can't wait to be violent


00:52:33.871 --> 00:52:35.672
and that comes out on the field.


00:52:35.672 --> 00:52:38.972
This kid, he acts like he doesn't want
to hit anyone.


00:52:39.072 --> 00:52:40.872
He's Ferdinand the Bull.


00:52:40.972 --> 00:52:42.972
- What?
- Nothing.


00:52:44.372 --> 00:52:45.872
I thought sure he was gonna be a player.


00:52:45.972 --> 00:52:48.873
I can't believe I used up my chiefs
to get him in school.


00:52:48.973 --> 00:52:52.173
I thought you said it was
your Christian duty?


00:52:52.873 --> 00:52:55.873
Look, Bert. He's never played before.


00:52:56.673 --> 00:53:00.274
And he won't this fall if he doesn't
improve a lot before then.


00:53:00.274 --> 00:53:02.374
Who xxx made him Bert bright?


00:53:03.174 --> 00:53:04.874
Unbelievable!


00:53:06.374 --> 00:53:08.175
Oh, God bless me.


00:53:08.575 --> 00:53:10.175
This is your summer workout sheet.


00:53:10.275 --> 00:53:13.375
Now, first it says to warm up
and get loose.


00:53:13.675 --> 00:53:15.675
Go ahead, get loose.


00:53:18.276 --> 00:53:19.576
Are you loose?


00:53:20.176 --> 00:53:23.976
Okay, next is five one hundred yard runs
to stretch out your legs.


00:53:24.076 --> 00:53:25.576
Let's go home,
play some video games.


00:53:25.676 --> 00:53:29.777
Look, everybody at Wingate is expecting
you to be a star football player.


00:53:29.877 --> 00:53:31.477
You don't want to let
them down, do you?


00:53:31.577 --> 00:53:32.277
I don’t know.


00:53:32.377 --> 00:53:33.677
What about Dad and Mom?


00:53:33.677 --> 00:53:36.677
'Cause you see, in our family
everyone's an athlete.


00:53:36.677 --> 00:53:38.377
Dad was a basketball star,


00:53:38.377 --> 00:53:40.678
Collins plays volleyball
and runs track.


00:53:40.778 --> 00:53:43.278
And me, as you know, I do it all.


00:53:43.378 --> 00:53:45.978
And Mom...
Mom was a cheerleader,


00:53:46.078 --> 00:53:49.178
which doesn't exactly count
but don't tell her I said that.


00:53:49.278 --> 00:53:50.579
- Okay?
- Okay.


00:53:50.679 --> 00:53:51.779
Okay.


00:53:54.479 --> 00:53:57.979
...fifty, fifty one,


00:53:59.279 --> 00:54:02.480
fifty two, fifty three...


00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:05.080
Come on and get it!
Go, go, go, go, go!


00:54:05.280 --> 00:54:07.880
Come on. Five seconds left in the game!


00:54:09.380 --> 00:54:11.680
Just like!
Just like!


00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:14.781
High knees, high knees, high knees!
xxx baby.


00:54:15.081 --> 00:54:16.581
Run like the wind!


00:54:18.081 --> 00:54:19.881
Go, Michael, go!


00:54:20.381 --> 00:54:23.282
...ninety eight, nine,


00:54:25.282 --> 00:54:26.482
one hundred.


00:54:26.482 --> 00:54:28.482
Move your feet! Move your feet!
Come on! Come on! Come on!


00:54:28.582 --> 00:54:30.382
Go. There you go.


00:54:30.582 --> 00:54:33.383
Get on the tackle!
Come on! Come on! Come on!


00:54:34.083 --> 00:54:35.983
Come on, Michael!


00:55:00.185 --> 00:55:01.285
Mrs. Tuohy?


00:55:01.385 --> 00:55:04.885
I hear "Mrs. Tuohy" I look over my
shoulder for my mother-in-law.


00:55:04.985 --> 00:55:08.386
Call me Leigh Anne or Mama
or almost anything else.


00:55:11.186 --> 00:55:14.186
- Can you help me get something?
- What?


00:55:16.487 --> 00:55:18.387
Driver's licence.


00:55:19.687 --> 00:55:23.887
Why do you need a driver's licence
when you don't even have a car?


00:55:30.388 --> 00:55:33.488
Michael, why do yo want
a driver's licence?


00:55:33.688 --> 00:55:36.688
Something to carry.
With my name on it.


00:55:43.489 --> 00:55:46.389
There's nobody named
Michael Oher in the system.


00:55:46.489 --> 00:55:48.790
Another last name perhaps?


00:55:51.090 --> 00:55:53.990
Look, I will sign something
that says he lives with us


00:55:53.990 --> 00:55:57.590
and we'll pay for all the insurance;
whatever it takes, okay?


00:55:58.090 --> 00:55:59.291
What's it gonna take?


00:55:59.391 --> 00:56:02.191
- You wanna do what?!
- You heard me.


00:56:02.291 --> 00:56:05.491
- Shouldn't we at least talk about this?
- What do you think we're doing?


00:56:05.591 --> 00:56:07.891
And don't act like I'm going
behind your back.


00:56:07.991 --> 00:56:11.692
I know you put us down as Michael's
medical contact at school.


00:56:11.692 --> 00:56:14.792
There's a huge difference between
paying for broken arm


00:56:14.892 --> 00:56:16.792
and being legally responsible
for someone.


00:56:16.792 --> 00:56:18.792
I mean the kid we barely know.


00:56:18.792 --> 00:56:22.093
That's another thing. We need
to find out more about his past.


00:56:22.193 --> 00:56:24.193
He won't talk about it.
He's like an onion,


00:56:24.193 --> 00:56:26.193
you have to peel him back
a layer at a time.


00:56:26.293 --> 00:56:28.393
Not if you use a knife.


00:56:29.393 --> 00:56:32.794
What if we took him to a child
psychologist or something?


00:56:32.794 --> 00:56:35.394
- Do you really expect Big Mike---
- "Michael"


00:56:35.494 --> 00:56:38.794
You really expect Michael to lie down
on a coach and talk about his childhood


00:56:38.894 --> 00:56:40.194
like he's Woody Allen or something?


00:56:40.194 --> 00:56:42.995
I mean, Michael's gift
is his ability to forget.


00:56:43.095 --> 00:56:47.495
He's mad at no one and he really
didn't care what happened in the past.


00:56:47.895 --> 00:56:49.495
You're right.


00:56:49.695 --> 00:56:51.195
Excuse me?


00:56:51.295 --> 00:56:52.895
"You're right?"


00:56:52.996 --> 00:56:55.596
How'd those words taste
coming out of your mouth?


00:56:55.696 --> 00:56:57.296
Like vinegar.


00:57:05.997 --> 00:57:08.797
At least promise me you'll think about it.


00:57:08.797 --> 00:57:10.297
Alright.


00:57:11.397 --> 00:57:14.698
"Alright" you'll think about it or
"alright" we should do it?


00:57:14.798 --> 00:57:16.898
Is there a difference?


00:57:19.298 --> 00:57:23.698
Just tell Gerald to hold on the chiffonier
and I'll get by after while.


00:57:24.998 --> 00:57:27.999
You don't...
I got to call you back. Bye.


00:57:30.699 --> 00:57:32.199
Excuse me.


00:57:33.699 --> 00:57:37.100
I'm not cutting, I'm just asking.
Let me tell you something, alright?


00:57:37.200 --> 00:57:39.200
We've been sitting around here
for over an hour


00:57:39.300 --> 00:57:41.100
and when I look around
and all I see


00:57:41.100 --> 00:57:43.700
is people shooting the bull
and drinking coffee.


00:57:43.800 --> 00:57:45.800
Who runs this place?


00:57:48.501 --> 00:57:50.901
Well, I'd have it in shape in two days,
I can tell you that.


00:57:51.001 --> 00:57:53.001
I'd bet you would.
How can I help you?


00:57:53.001 --> 00:57:55.201
- Oh, he was first.
- No, you go ahead.


00:57:55.301 --> 00:57:57.702
- I think I want to hear this
- Me too.


00:57:57.702 --> 00:57:59.402
I do not appreciate
the attitude.


00:57:59.502 --> 00:58:02.402
Ma'am,
now you can tell me what you want


00:58:02.702 --> 00:58:04.902
or I'll make sure you wait all day.


00:58:04.902 --> 00:58:06.902
Now how can I help you?


00:58:07.002 --> 00:58:09.003
I'd like to become
a legal guardian.


00:58:09.003 --> 00:58:11.103
Lord help that child.


00:58:14.803 --> 00:58:19.004
There's very little on Michael.
Most of his files have been lost.


00:58:19.404 --> 00:58:22.504
- What is in there?
- A few case notes.


00:58:22.804 --> 00:58:27.504
This one describes an incident where
Officers forcibly removed Michael


00:58:27.604 --> 00:58:30.405
from Denise Oher's care
when Michael was seven.


00:58:30.405 --> 00:58:33.205
Quite a scene evidently.
They had to split up the kids.


00:58:33.305 --> 00:58:34.805
And it's far from the worst.


00:58:34.805 --> 00:58:36.905
Where is she? His mother?


00:58:36.905 --> 00:58:41.406
Dunno, if you find her we got
a bunch more files we could add to.


00:58:42.406 --> 00:58:45.806
- How many kids does she have?
- At least a dozen, probably.


00:58:45.806 --> 00:58:48.206
If not more.
With her drug arrest record


00:58:48.306 --> 00:58:50.906
my guess would be
she can't even remember.


00:58:51.307 --> 00:58:53.107
May I see that?


00:58:57.507 --> 00:59:00.107
So we'd need her permission, right?


00:59:00.107 --> 00:59:02.308
No. Michael is a ward of the state.


00:59:02.308 --> 00:59:05.508
Just apply and get a Judge
to sign off on it.


00:59:07.608 --> 00:59:11.808
So you would just give him away
without even telling his mother?


00:59:35.411 --> 00:59:36.811
Mrs. Oher?


00:59:40.311 --> 00:59:41.811
Hi.


00:59:41.911 --> 00:59:43.411
Mrs. Oher?


00:59:45.012 --> 00:59:47.312
- You from the state?
- No.


00:59:48.412 --> 00:59:54.012
My name is Leigh Anne Tuohy
and your son Michael lives with me.


00:59:55.513 --> 00:59:57.213
And my family.


01:00:03.713 --> 01:00:06.614
How's my boy? How's big Mike?


01:00:07.114 --> 01:00:09.714
He's fine. He's doing really well.


01:00:10.914 --> 01:00:13.314
We might have some wine
in the kitchen, if you...


01:00:13.414 --> 01:00:15.714
Oh, no, no, no.
That's really kind.


01:00:16.014 --> 01:00:18.115
When did you last see Michael?


01:00:19.415 --> 01:00:20.915
I don't know.


01:00:21.615 --> 01:00:24.715
How many foster kids you got
living with you?


01:00:25.915 --> 01:00:29.916
Oh, I'm not a foster parent to Michael.
We were just helping him out.


01:00:30.316 --> 01:00:33.616
- State don't pay you nothing?
- No.


01:00:34.116 --> 01:00:37.316
And you feed him?
You buy him clothes, too?


01:00:37.616 --> 01:00:41.017
Well, when I can find them in his size.


01:00:44.017 --> 01:00:46.417
You a fine Christian lady.


01:00:46.817 --> 01:00:48.317
Well I try to be.


01:00:50.418 --> 01:00:52.918
This is all really nice
what you're doing,


01:00:53.018 --> 01:00:56.418
but don't be surprised if one day
you wake up and he gone.


01:00:57.618 --> 01:01:00.119
- What do you mean?
- He's a "runner."


01:01:01.019 --> 01:01:04.619
That's what the state called him
after they took him from me.


01:01:06.319 --> 01:01:08.719
Every foster home they sent him to,


01:01:09.619 --> 01:01:13.020
he'd slip out the window at night
and come looking for me.


01:01:13.020 --> 01:01:17.920
No matter where I was that boy would
come find me, take care of me.


01:01:20.120 --> 01:01:22.821
I've had some health problems.


01:01:24.921 --> 01:01:28.921
Mrs. Oher, was Michael born
under a different name?


01:01:29.921 --> 01:01:33.522
Proctor. That was his Daddy's last name.


01:01:34.422 --> 01:01:37.422
- Where is he?
- Ain't seen him since he left.


01:01:38.122 --> 01:01:39.622
And when was that?


01:01:39.922 --> 01:01:42.022
Week after was Mike born?


01:01:43.023 --> 01:01:45.623
Do you have his birth certificate?


01:01:53.223 --> 01:01:55.724
It's alright. I'll figure it out.


01:02:10.925 --> 01:02:13.625
Mrs. Oher, you'll always
be Michael's Mama.


01:02:17.926 --> 01:02:19.426
Would you like to see him?


01:02:19.426 --> 01:02:22.326
No. Not this way.


01:02:25.626 --> 01:02:27.127
It's Williams.


01:02:29.427 --> 01:02:31.327
His last name's Williams.


01:02:33.627 --> 01:02:36.528
Couldn't even remember
who the boy's father is.


01:03:06.430 --> 01:03:09.231
The color is better, the graphic is bright.
It's awesome!


01:03:09.331 --> 01:03:12.231
Michael, we have something
we'd like to ask you.


01:03:12.731 --> 01:03:14.231
What?


01:03:15.131 --> 01:03:16.831
Leigh Anne and I, we...


01:03:17.531 --> 01:03:19.031
Well...


01:03:19.431 --> 01:03:22.032
We'd like to become your legal guardians.


01:03:22.032 --> 01:03:23.532
What's that mean?


01:03:23.532 --> 01:03:26.432
What it means is, that we want to know


01:03:26.632 --> 01:03:29.432
if you'd like to become
a part of this family?


01:03:38.733 --> 01:03:40.833
I kinda thought I already was.


01:03:49.534 --> 01:03:51.634
Well alright then.


01:03:59.835 --> 01:04:01.335
Right here.


01:04:05.236 --> 01:04:06.736
We got a couple of steps.


01:04:06.736 --> 01:04:09.036
- Watch your big foot.
- One more.


01:04:09.836 --> 01:04:11.936
One more. There we go.


01:04:13.437 --> 01:04:15.537
Alright. Take off the belt.


01:04:19.837 --> 01:04:22.637
Well, that's the one you want it,
didn't it?


01:04:24.638 --> 01:04:27.738
Here. Here you go.
Go ahead. Take it for a ride. Go.


01:04:28.138 --> 01:04:29.438
- Can I go too?
- Yeah.


01:04:29.438 --> 01:04:31.338
Michael? Be careful.


01:04:31.438 --> 01:04:33.438
xxx


01:04:36.239 --> 01:04:39.639
- He wanted a truck?!
- Michael thinks he's a redneck.


01:04:39.839 --> 01:04:41.339
Come on, Michael!


01:04:42.339 --> 01:04:46.240
Okay. See, you're the ketchup, here
at Left Tackle. On the weakside.


01:04:46.340 --> 01:04:48.540
The fist play is simple. "Gap."


01:04:51.240 --> 01:04:55.440
Now, see, dishes means you're going
to block whoever is in front of you,


01:04:55.540 --> 01:04:58.741
or on your inside shoulder if you're not
covered by a defender.


01:04:58.841 --> 01:05:02.641
Now, I'll be the running back and you
show me what you're supposed to do.


01:05:02.641 --> 01:05:04.141
Ready.... Hike!


01:05:04.541 --> 01:05:07.142
You block him, you hit him,


01:05:07.242 --> 01:05:10.542
quarterback will hand it off,
he gets the ball and...


01:05:10.742 --> 01:05:13.542
Open lane to the end zone.
All there is to it.


01:05:13.542 --> 01:05:15.442
What's going on here?!


01:05:15.642 --> 01:05:17.342
Player Spice just scored.


01:05:17.342 --> 01:05:20.343
We're going through the playbook.
Michael got move to offense.


01:05:20.343 --> 01:05:23.243
Yeah. Well, when you're done, please,
put the players back in the spice cabinet.


01:05:23.343 --> 01:05:25.143
- Thank you.
- No problem.


01:05:25.943 --> 01:05:29.144
Oh, actually, Mom, we were
kinda waiting for you.


01:05:29.644 --> 01:05:34.044
You see, the new Madden game came out
and me and Michael wanted to go get it.


01:05:34.244 --> 01:05:35.944
I can't, baby. I've got a meeting
in ten minutes


01:05:35.944 --> 01:05:37.444
But he can drive!


01:05:38.144 --> 01:05:39.845
He can drive us.


01:05:42.045 --> 01:05:44.545
Oh, yeah.
That's what I'm talking about.


01:05:44.645 --> 01:05:46.945
- What do you know about this?
- I already know all about this!


01:05:46.945 --> 01:05:49.345
- Alright, show me something.
- I'll tell you something, alright?


01:05:49.345 --> 01:05:51.546
I'll start it. Follow my leads.


01:05:51.746 --> 01:05:53.046
- Ready?
- Yes.


01:05:53.246 --> 01:05:55.246
# Next days function,
high class luncheon #


01:05:55.346 --> 01:05:57.246
# Food is served
and you're stone cold munchin' #


01:05:57.346 --> 01:05:59.046
# Music comes on,
people start to dance #


01:05:59.146 --> 01:06:01.147
# But then you ate so much
you nearly split your pants #


01:06:01.147 --> 01:06:03.447
# A girl starts walkin,
guys start gawkin' #


01:06:03.447 --> 01:06:05.347
# Sits down next to you
and starts talkin' #


01:06:05.347 --> 01:06:07.247
# Says she wanna dance
cus she likes the groove #


01:06:07.347 --> 01:06:09.847
# So come on fatso
and just bust a move #


01:06:09.847 --> 01:06:13.348
# If you want it, you've got it #


01:06:14.148 --> 01:06:17.348
# if you want it baby you got it #


01:06:18.248 --> 01:06:21.748
# If you want it, you've got it #


01:06:22.349 --> 01:06:25.449
# if you want it baby you got it #


01:06:29.849 --> 01:06:32.850
This is not a 40.000 dollar Oushak,
Omeed.


01:06:32.850 --> 01:06:34.450
You're crazy, Leigh Anne!


01:06:34.550 --> 01:06:37.750
The borders have different width.
They've been altered.


01:06:37.850 --> 01:06:40.650
We'll give you seventeen tops, alright?


01:06:40.850 --> 01:06:42.350
Hello?


01:06:45.851 --> 01:06:47.751
Hey, hey, ma'am.
Ma'am, we check it.


01:06:47.751 --> 01:06:50.251
Those are my kids. Those are my kids!


01:06:52.651 --> 01:06:54.051
Oh my God!


01:06:54.552 --> 01:06:55.652
- It will be okay.
- Where are they?


01:06:55.752 --> 01:06:57.152
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry.
Oh my God!


01:06:57.252 --> 01:06:58.952
- Michael, you okay?
- I'm fine. SJ!


01:06:59.052 --> 01:07:01.552
- Michael, you're alright?
- Go help SJ!


01:07:02.152 --> 01:07:04.252
I'm so sorry - so sorry!


01:07:07.053 --> 01:07:08.353
Excuse me, ma'am?


01:07:08.453 --> 01:07:09.953
SJ! SJ!


01:07:11.153 --> 01:07:12.753
- Mom?
- Yes, baby?


01:07:12.953 --> 01:07:15.954
Do you think the blood will come
out of my shirt?


01:07:16.754 --> 01:07:19.854
Yes, I think the blood will come
out of your shirt.


01:07:20.154 --> 01:07:22.454
Ma'am, an airbag deploys
at 200 miles an hour.


01:07:22.554 --> 01:07:24.154
Your son's too small to sit
in the front seat.


01:07:24.254 --> 01:07:26.054
But he's okay, right?


01:07:26.254 --> 01:07:27.555
Busted lip, bruised face.


01:07:27.655 --> 01:07:29.655
Usually when someone his size
gets the airbag


01:07:29.755 --> 01:07:32.055
it's fractured faces, a broken neck.


01:07:32.055 --> 01:07:33.355
Maybe worse.


01:07:33.455 --> 01:07:36.855
Like the air bag was coming at him
then changed direction.


01:07:36.955 --> 01:07:39.556
Quiet defective or something like that.


01:07:39.556 --> 01:07:41.556
Your son's very, very lucky.


01:07:41.756 --> 01:07:44.956
No idea. I called the insurance.
He's fine. He's fine!


01:07:45.456 --> 01:07:48.057
I'll talk to you later.
I got to go. Bye.


01:07:51.157 --> 01:07:53.157
SJ's fine.


01:07:54.157 --> 01:07:58.357
He is. He's actually enjoying all
the attention he's getting back there.


01:08:00.058 --> 01:08:03.958
Hey, Michael. Could happen to anyone,
alright? It's not your fault.


01:08:05.358 --> 01:08:06.958
Honey, look at me.


01:08:13.059 --> 01:08:15.359
Michael, what happened to your arm?


01:08:16.659 --> 01:08:18.859
I stopped it.


01:08:37.061 --> 01:08:38.761
Let's go!


01:08:44.062 --> 01:08:46.562
Oher! You've got a hundred pounds
on Collis


01:08:46.662 --> 01:08:48.962
and you can't keep him out
of our backfield?!


01:08:48.962 --> 01:08:51.962
Hold your block until the whistle blow.
Hold it!


01:08:51.962 --> 01:08:53.463
Alright, let's go!


01:08:54.363 --> 01:08:55.863
What's with the camera?


01:08:55.863 --> 01:08:59.963
Michael always does better when he sees
what he's supposed to be doing.

